From: Xiaomi Mi MIX Linux port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: xiaomi-lithium: headphones on their own stream

Speaker and headphones shared the MultiMedia1 front end, so UCM had to put
them in separate (conflicting) profiles and every jack event made PipeWire
switch profiles, closing and reopening the PCM. Through its per-UCM
"_ucmNNNN." PCM names that reopen intermittently failed with -EINVAL and
left only a dummy output.

Add MultiMedia2 (hw:N,1) for the headphones. With a back end routed to each
front end for the whole verb, both outputs are sinks of one profile and a
jack event only changes the preferred sink. Tested on hardware with the
matching UCM (device package r13).

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-lithium.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996pro-xiaomi-lithium.dts
@@ -805,6 +805,7 @@
 
 &q6asmdai {
 	dai@0 { reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA1>; };
+	dai@1 { reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>; };
 };
 
 &sound {
@@ -821,6 +822,12 @@
 		cpu { sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA1>; };
 	};
 
+	/* Headphones get their own stream: speaker and headphones are separate PCMs */
+	mm2-dai-link {
+		link-name = "MultiMedia2";
+		cpu { sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>; };
+	};
+
 	wcd-aif1-pb-dai-link {
 		link-name = "AIF1_PB";
 		cpu { sound-dai = <&q6afedai SLIMBUS_4_RX>; };
